<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμιος</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			6.73
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Maced.
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			Man.
			5.161
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νομεύς</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of shepherds,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. θεός</span> the <i>pastoral</i> god,
			i.e. Pan, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Pan.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.96
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Eryc.
			</span></i>); of Apollo, as shepherd of Admetus, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				47
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1218
			</span></i> (but also, <i>god of Law</i> (cf. sq.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rendic.Linc.</u>
				1925.419
			</span></i> (Cyrene, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>, dedic. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νομοφύλακες</span>)); of Aristaeus, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				9.65
			</span></i>; of Hermes, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				977
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				16
			</span></i>; of Dionysus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.524.14
			</span></i>; of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Archyt.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.1.138
			</span></i> (expld. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέμω</span>); of the
			Nymphs, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				51.12
			</span></i>; N. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρη,</span> in Arcadia, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				8.3.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. μέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.578
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Clearch.
					37
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. φορβάς</span> Epic.in<i><span class="en">
				<u>BKT</u>
				5(1).112
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμιον, τό,</span>
			<i>pasturedues,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PStrassb.
				21.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>.</div>
